   I played a Unix version of Omega for a very brief while, and found a
few things which allow you to get a good start without a powerhouse
character.  (I tended to play myself - a pencil-necked geek with STR 9,
Power 4, etc).  Anyway, neat things you could do:
   Very first little goblin you run into (hopefully not a chieftain)
Talk/Threaten him.  Usually this is very easy to do.  He cowers, and
you have the option to Kill him anyway.  Very easy, and highly chaotic.
And you get all the XP too.
   Now that you are chaotic, you can run back to the temple and become
an acolyte of Set or somesuch.  That done, you take a little swim in
the nearby Sea of Chaos, and you get hordes of XP that way.  After a
little while, you would also be able to Threaten and Backstab the
goblin chieftains as well.
   Unfortunately, the machine I played on has been down for months,
so I can't say much of anything else.
   Other neat little trick:  First chance you get, give the local
charity a few cents.  You are suddenly lawful good enough to be a
paladin.  Sign up, get your free horse, and continue as above.

Tally-ho.

